==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|sentiēns||feeling, perceiving}}, present active participle of {{m|la|sentiō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɛnʃənt/|/ˈsɛntiənt/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Experiencing [[sensation]], [[thought]], or [[feeling]].
# Able to consciously [[perceive]] through the use of [[sense]] faculties.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|in|_|science fiction}} Possessing human-like awareness and intelligence.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|able to perceive}} {{l|en|sensate}}
* {{sense|human-like awareness}} {{l|en|intelligent}}, {{l|en|sapient}},  {{l|en|self-aware}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|able to perceive}} {{l|en|insensate}}

